WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.000
PhysRL3D. Beyond visual appearance.
Physical objectives, built into the generator.

00:03.000 --> 00:09.000
Selected real print: TRELLIS.2 falls; PhysRL3D-SAS stands.
Source plays at 0.5×; the final frame is held.

00:09.000 --> 00:15.000
Standability, material efficiency and geometric fidelity.
Improving one objective can compromise the others.

00:15.000 --> 00:23.000
Christmas tree: 18.91 g to 14.06 g total, including supports.
Slicer estimates; support removal is an illustrative animation.

00:23.000 --> 00:33.000
Post-train the first stage with DiffusionNFT and SAS.
Online rewards require no simulator or slicer queries.

00:33.000 --> 00:44.000
HY3D-Bench: 84.8% to 98.2% standability; 11.8% less total material.
Three-seed averages, not a guarantee for every object.

00:44.000 --> 00:50.000
PhysRL3D. Explore the evidence at physrl3d.github.io.
